message: "If you use this work, software, or theoretical framework, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Profinite Memory Tensor (M): Overcoming Arrhenius Model Collapse in Non-Linear NTC Cold Flames"
abstract: >-
  Predictive models in non-linear kinetics and fluid dynamics collapse during regime transitions 
  such as the Negative Temperature Coefficient (NTC) cold flame region (T = 840–920 K), 
  where Arrhenius kinetics exhibits a 51.10% relative error due to blindness toward local 
  arrow-of-time inversions. This repository implements the Profinite Memory Tensor (M) framework, 
  unifying inverse limits, Young measures, and a topological trace operator (H) governed by a 
  Dirac jump condition. Validated across 814 reaction conditions in Cantera (GRI-Mech 3.0), it 
  reduces transition error to 1.37% (RMSE = 0.0500, R² = 0.9900) and detects entropy "arrow"
  inversion through a sign flip in H (from -0.213 to +0.951), with jump continuity in weak 
  solutions formally machine-checked in Lean 4.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Antonio
    family-names: García Poujol

